Ladybird skips indexed reads and writes when the receiver has fewer
than two elements. The sort algorithm in Ecma-262 calls Set for each
sorted element, including the only element in a frozen singleton.

V8 checks the length in ArrayPrototypeSort, SpiderMonkey checks it
in ArraySortPrologue, and JavaScriptCore checks it in sortImpl.
Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 returned frozen
singletons and array-like receivers after reading only their length.
All three rejected an invalid comparator before reading the length.
